**Q: How can I implement a smoothly eased interpolation between two Vector3 points in Unity using the smoothstep function instead of linear interpolation?**

**A:** You can create a helper function that normalizes your input `t` and applies `Mathf.SmoothStep`, then uses the result to interpolate between the start and end positions via `Vector3.Lerp`:

```csharp
public static Vector3 SmoothLerp(Vector3 start, Vector3 end, float t)
{
    // Clamp t to ensure it stays within [0, 1] for safety
    t = Mathf.Clamp01(t);

    // Apply smoothstep easing curve
    float easedT = Mathf.SmoothStep(0f, 1f, t);

    return Vector3.Lerp(start, end, easedT);
}
```

